{\n  \"merge-pdf\": {\n    \"definition\": \"PDF merging is the process of combining multiple independent PDF documents into a single cohesive Portable Document Format (PDF) file.\",\n    \"purpose\": \"It is used to organize fragmented documents, merge scanned reports, combine project attachments, and simplify document sharing by reducing the number of individual attachments.\",\n    \"how_works\": \"The tool reads the binary content of each uploaded PDF, parses the page catalogs using client-side JavaScript (PDF-Lib), reorders them according to user preference, and compiles them into a new unified pages stream, saving the resulting document directly to the client device.\",\n    \"benefits\": [\n      \"Zero server uploads: Complete privacy and compliance with data safety standards.\",\n      \"Instant client-side processing: High-speed operation running locally in the browser.\",\n      \"Custom page sorting: Drag and drop pages to change sequence before compiling.\",\n      \"Works on all devices: Responsive HTML5 interface compatible with desktop, mobile, and tablets.\"\n    ],\n    \"limitations\": [\n      \"Encrypted files: Passwords must be removed using the Unlock PDF tool before merging.\",\n      \"Browser memory: Extremely large mergers (e.g. 50+ files of 50MB each) may exceed local browser memory limits.\"\n    ],\n    \"examples\": [\n      {\n        \"before\": \"Document_A.pdf (4 pages) + Document_B.pdf (6 pages) + Document_C.pdf (2 pages)\",\n        \"after\": \"Unified_Document.pdf (12 pages)\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"faqs\": [\n      {\"q\": \"Is my data uploaded to any server?\", \"a\": \"No, all document operations execute strictly within your local browser sandbox. No file data is sent to external servers.\"},\n      {\"q\": \"How many PDFs can I combine?\", \"a\": \"You can merge up to 50 PDF files simultaneously. The individual file size limit is 50MB.\"},\n      {\"q\": \"Does merging compromise hyperlink structure?\", \"a\": \"No, standard PDF pages merging preserves internal page re